END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Learn to SUP: Build skills. Find flow. Love the river.
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260613T110000
UID:11b9b22420e592ffcfe7e7962b84751a@thefloathousepetaluma.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/63
 02d39abd02437a9e9f0276/1771550281507-265ECDHT7D3N331PAKVN/Learn+to+SUP+wit
 h+us++2026+Squarespace+image+%281500+x+1000+px%29.png
DESCRIPTION:Learn to SUP: We’re here to help you build skills and find f
 low. Ready to feel confident on a paddleboard? Our Learn to SUP class is a
  welcoming\, two-hour introduction designed to help you paddle smarter —
  not harder — so you can truly enjoy your time on the water. Start your 
 SUP journey here. For just $60 \, you’ll learn from an ACA-certified (Am
 erican Canoe Association) instructor in a small\, supportive group of just
  2–6 students . That means personalized attention\, real feedback\, and 
 space to grow. We’ll cover: Proper stance and balance Efficient paddle t
 echnique Turning and maneuvering Launching and returning to the dock River
  awareness and safety basics Many people hop on a board and think they’r
 e having fun — but they’re working twice as hard as they need to. This
  class unlocks the “aha” moments that make paddleboarding smoother\, m
 ore efficient\, and way more enjoyable. Held right in the heart of downtow
 n Petaluma on the beautiful Petaluma River\, this is your chance to build 
 skills in a calm\, supportive environment — and start feeling at home on
  the water. Bring a friend\, learn together\, and find your flow. All equi
 pment included. Only 6 paddlers per class. Book your spot early. #block-a6
